I did some source diving to try to figure this out.  Line
272 of dig.c seems to be the crucial part:

  digging.effort += 10 + rn2(5) + abon() +
    uwep->spe - greatest_erosion(uwep) + u.udaminc;

So no mention of any difference between pickaxe and mattock.
In include/obj.c is a check to see if it can be used to dig:

#define is_pick(otmp)   ((otmp->oclass == WEAPON_CLASS || \
                         otmp->oclass == TOOL_CLASS) && \
                         objects[otmp->otyp].oc_skill == P_PICK_AXE)

Which gives a yes for anything in the skill class of
pickaxe, again no numerical difference in digging rate.
Also no sign of a difference in objects.c:

/* axe-type */
...
WEAPON("dwarvish mattock", "broad pick",
        0, 0, 1, 13,120, 50, 12,  8,-1, B,   P_PICK_AXE, IRON,
HI_METAL),
...
/* tools useful as weapons */
WEPTOOL("pick-axe", (char *)0,
        1, 0, 0, 20, 100,  50,  6,  3, WHACK,  P_PICK_AXE, IRON,
HI_METAL),

So it appears to me that the differences between a pickaxe
and a dwarvish mattock are one-vs-two handed, combat damage,
and weight, but no difference in digging effort.



